## Q3: Companies That Have Addressed the Data Scarcity Problem

### Startups

**ChipAgents (founded 2024, $74M raised Feb 2026)**
- Focus: Agentic AI for RTL design, verification, and waveform debugging (pre-silicon).
- Claims 80% higher verification productivity; deployed at 50 semiconductor companies.
- Their "Waveform Agents" is the closest analog to post-silicon link training diagnosis, but published details on how they handle data scarcity for post-silicon root-cause classification are not public.
- Backed by Bessemer, Micron Ventures, MediaTek, Ericsson, Matter Venture Partners (TSMC-backed).

Sources: [Businesswire](https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260217568914/en/ChipAgents-Raises-$74M-to-Scale-an-Agentic-AI-Platform-to-Accelerate-Chip-Design), [Semiwiki](https://semiwiki.com/eda/chipagents-ai/361025-ai-powered-waveform-debugging-revolutionizing-semiconductor-verification/)

**SixSense (founded 2018, $8.5M Series A, July 2025)**
- Focus: Visual inspection and defect classification for semiconductor manufacturing (wafer/die level).
- Claims models deployable in under two days using fab-specific data — minimal labeled data required.
- Over 100 million chips processed at GlobalFoundries, JCET.
- Addresses wafer-level defect classification data scarcity via transfer learning and intelligent annotation; not post-silicon link training debug.

Sources: [TechCrunch](https://techcrunch.com/2025/07/31/female-founded-semiconductor-ai-startup-sixsense-raises-funding/), [SEMI](https://www.semi.org/en/sea-newsletter-sixsense-automates-visual-inspection-to-boost-chip-defect-detection-and-classification-accuracy)

---

### Incumbents

**NVIDIA**
- Uses SSL + fine-tuning for wafer defect classification (NV-DINOv2), achieving near-expert accuracy with ~600 labeled examples.
- For post-silicon GPU hardware reliability during Llama 3 training (466 interruptions in 54 days, 78% hardware-caused): deployed Fleetscanner, Ripple, and Hardware Sentinel. This is runtime **anomaly detection**, not root-cause classification ML.

Sources: [NVIDIA failure analysis blog](https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/failure-analysis-lab-nvidia-life/), [Meta engineering](https://engineering.fb.com/2025/07/22/data-infrastructure/how-meta-keeps-its-ai-hardware-reliable/)

**Intel**
- Adaptive test selection (pass/fail outcomes), not root-cause classification.
- ML tools for performance counter–based anomaly detection in CPU/GPU validation.
- Proprietary labeled failure datasets exist internally but are not disclosed.

**Synopsys**
- Verdi RDA uses unsupervised ML for simulation regression binning (90% accuracy), avoiding labeled data dependency.
- AI-driven debug automation via TraceDiff (waveform comparison), not ML classification over labeled failure corpora.

Sources: [Synopsys Verdi RDA datasheet](https://www.synopsys.com/verification/resources/datasheets/verdi-rda-datasheet.html)

**Keysight (acquired Spirent, 2025)**
- Dominant in CXL/PCIe protocol analyzer hardware (up to 16 GB trace buffers, all PCIe generations through 7.0, CXL 3.x).
- Provides tooling infrastructure for capture and analysis of link training failures.
- **No published AI/ML root-cause classification layer for CXL/PCIe link training failures** — analysis remains expert-driven.

Sources: [Keysight PCIe analyzers](https://www.keysight.com/zz/en/products/digital-protocol-analyzers/pcie-protocol-analyzers.html)

